olspan="1">1,237 (38.9)</td></tr><tr><td colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1">Race/ethnicity</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;White (non-Hispanic)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1,033 (47.0)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">371 (44.5)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">92 (59.7)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1,496 (47.0)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Hispanic or Latino</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">448 (20.4)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">143 (17.2)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28 (18.2)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">619 (19.4)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Asian</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">416 (18.9)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">173 (20.7)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">16 (10.4)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">605 (19.0)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Black (non-Hispanic)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">155 (7.1)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">98 (11.8)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7 (4.6)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">260 (8.2)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Multiple races/other</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">144 (6.6)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">49 (5.9)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">11 (7.1)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">204 (6.4)</td></tr><tr><td colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1">Interview type</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Proxy</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2,003 (91.2)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">441 (52.9)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">59 (38.3)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2,503 (78.6)</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02003;Self</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">193 (8.8)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">393 (47.1)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">95 (61.7)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">681 (21.4)</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn1-ehp-116-1383"><label>a</label><p>This category consists of 74 youths who worked in rescue/recovery and 80 passers-by south of Chambers Street on the morning of 11 September 2001.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="t2-ehp-116-1383" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Symptoms and conditions that began or worsened after 9/11, by age on 9/11, among 3,184<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn2-ehp-116-1383">a</xref> children enrolled in the WTCHR, September 2003 through November 2004 [no. (%)].</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th colspan="4" align="center" rowspan="1">Age on 9/11 (years)<hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Symptom/characteristic</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0&#x02013;4</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5&#x02013;11</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">12&#x02013;17</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Total</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">No.</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">875<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn2-ehp-116-1383">a</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1,072<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn2-ehp-116-1383">a</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1,237<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn2-ehp-116-1383">a</xref></td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3,184<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn2-ehp-116-1383">a</xref></td></tr><tr><td colspan="5" align="left" rowspan="1">Injuries on 9/11</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowsp